course: dictionary
lesson: 4626
title: Hikers on the trail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hiker is a person who goes on long walks in the country, in the hills or up mountains, for fun or exercise. You can spot the word's job from the clues: a hiker walks a long way, usually away from roads. «Fog and dark can make even a short walk confusing, so hikers stay together and tell someone their route.» The clues are fog, dark and confusing, so a hiker must plan carefully and stay safe.
explain: Context shows you what a word does in a sentence. Here «hikers» is the subject, the people who stay together and tell someone where they are going. Try the swap check: put «walkers» in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does, but a hiker is a walker on a long trail far from home.
explain: In bear country, «hikers stay in groups, talk or make noise so bears hear them coming». The word «so» is a clue: it tells you why they do this. Hikers make noise to avoid surprising a bear, which is a good example of how the context explains an action.
fact: A hiker is a person who goes on long walks in the country, hills or mountains.
fact: The plural of hiker is hikers, as in «hikers stay together».
fact: Hikers carry water, a map and warm clothes, and they tell someone where they are going.
fact: «Ötzi the Iceman» lived about 5,300 years ago, and was found by hikers in 1991 in the Alps.
fact: In bear country, hikers stay in groups and make noise so bears hear them coming.
exercise: «Heat and too little water can make hikers very ill quickly.» Why do hikers need to carry water? | To keep it as a pet | *So they stay well, because heat and too little water can make them very ill | To wash their hair on the trail | To make their bags heavier for fun
exercise: What is a hiker? | A shop worker who sells maps | A bird that lives high in the trees | A person who drives a car on a motorway | *A person who goes on long walks in the country or hills
exercise: «Ötzi the Iceman lived about 5,300 years ago and was found by hikers in 1991.» Find and copy the word that tells who found him. | Ötzi | Alps | *hikers | ice
test: «In bear country, hikers keep food locked away and never run from a bear.» Why do hikers keep food locked away? | To give the food to the bears as a treat | *So bears do not come looking for food near people | Because food is too heavy to carry | To make the food taste better on the trail
test: In the story, a hiker walked closer to a mother moose with a calf. Which hiker was charged? | *The hiker who had not noticed the moose | Ötzi the Iceman | The hikers who stayed in groups | The girl in Montana who turned back
exam: Why do hikers stay together and tell someone their route? | *Fog and dark can make a walk confusing, so it is safer | Because a route never changes once you start | To make the walk longer and more fun for everyone | Because hikers like getting lost in the hills
